- Prefer stateless edge components + regional data stores
- Minimize PII; IPs may be truncated/hashed; configurable retention for analytics (e.g., 7–30 days)
- Small platform team: operational simplicity is a first-class goal

---

## Simplified Architecture

This system uses:
- An **edge rate limiter** (library/filter) with an in-process L1 cache for microsecond decisions.
- A **regional rate limit service** that owns atomic counter updates and regional budget management.
- A **single Postgres-backed control plane** that stores policies, publishes immutable snapshots, and coordinates regional budgets for global limits.
- Standard metrics/tracing plus sampled decision logs for debugging and abuse analysis.

### High-Level Component Diagram

```mermaid
graph TB
  subgraph EL[Edge Layer (per POP)]
    GW[API Gateway / Edge Proxy]
    RL[Rate Limiter Filter / Library]
    L1[(L1 In-Memory Buckets)]
  end

  subgraph RLAYER[Regional Layer (per Region)]
    RLS[Regional Rate Limit Service]
    RKV[(Regional KV: Redis/KeyDB)]
    SC[Snapshot Cache (in RLS)]
  end

  subgraph CP[Global Control Plane]
    CPS[Control Plane Service (Policies + Budget Coordinator)]
    PDB[(Postgres: policies + snapshots + budget state)]
  end

  subgraph OBS[Observability]
